Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-30
Subject: Use the implicit pshortstring alias
License: expat

`cutils.stringdispose` takes a `var p: pshortstring` parameter.  With the
local declaration, that parameter has the distinct `cutils.pshortstring`
type, while callers pass variables declared as bare `pshortstring` in
their own units.  Remove the local declaration so the formal parameter and
callers use the same implicit `pshortstring` type.

Later FPC compiler trees already use `pshortstring` without declaring a
local alias in `compiler/cutils.pas`.

--- a/compiler/cutils.pas
+++ b/compiler/cutils.pas
@@ -31,7 +31,6 @@ interface
 
 
     type
-       pshortstring = ^string;
        Tcharset=set of char;
 
     var
